    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 6e1805bfd: the bug does not reproduce without a change.\n\nEvidence:\n- I wrote a pin in `crates/post/tests/script_wire_iso.rs`. It posts one wire section through `engine::run` with `PARAM OriginX` (and `OriginY`) set to `null`, `\"nan\"` and `\"inf\"`.\n- On unchanged code the post does not run the script. `engine::run` returns `Refused(\"stream parameter OriginX must be a finite number\")`. No program is written, so the file is blocked.\n- The guard is in `crates/post/src/post/wcs_rotate.rs:143-144` (`read_finite`). `engine::run_program_with` calls `wcs_rotate::apply` at `crates/post/src/post/engine.rs:140` for each post, before any script hook.\n- The engine is the only path that runs the script hooks. So the skip in `wire-iso.cps` lines 199-200 cannot be reached with a non-finite origin.\n\nThe guard came in commit 84583da67 (`fix(wcs): carry Z-rotated work offset through generation and post`, #760).\n\nSuggest closing; the maintainer decides. A script-level guard in `wire-iso.cps` would be defence in depth only. I did not open a PR for it.\n\nClaim released.\n",
